      ],
      "source": "https://www.sewickleyhistory.online/our-sewickley/leetsdale-borough/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After the Depreciation Lands were sold in Philadelphia in 1786, Daniel Leet bought tracts 3‑9 that now form Leetsdale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leetsdale%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Beaver Road, once a Native American trail, became a state road in 1809 and drew stagecoach traffic through Leetsdale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leetsdale%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Harmony Brickworks, opened in 1888, fired about 20,000 red bricks a day for the region.",
